## Overview
#c1[overview,i5] Ky executes HTTP requests via fetch, returning a ResponsePromise that combines standard Promise behavior with convenience body shortcuts.
  > source/types/ResponsePromise.ts::ResponsePromise #2ce0b174e51b
  > source/utils/timeout.ts::timeout #253b066c01c5
#c2[overview,i5] Ky creates and extends client instances using deep-merging, where replaceOption or explicit undefined can override default merge semantics.
  > readme.md:1019 #25512816a67a
  > readme.md::replaceOption #72ebac56a0ef
  > source/index.ts::createInstance #748a39d6aa23
  > source/types/ky.ts:83 #74a04919adda
  > source/types/ky.ts:100 #0092cc46e569
  > source/utils/merge.ts::validateAndMerge #39a197429568
#c3[overview,i5] Synchronous init hooks run during request setup; their errors and invalid options reject the ResponsePromise directly without invoking beforeError hooks.
  > readme.md::hooks.init #6923bdd6675e
  > source/index.ts:16 #5e01cc2a5e41
  > source/index.ts::createRequest.of #664943d55fd7
  > source/core/Ky.ts::cloneInitHookOptions #0d6fe249e71f
  > source/types/ResponsePromise.ts:4 #fd5e769bd4b3
  > source/types/hooks.ts:10 #74bfbd7ef100
#c4[overview,i5] Ky automatically retries eligible failed requests and network errors up to a configured limit, respecting retry timing headers, delays, and backoff limits.
  > readme.md:264-266 #0e45ffca8cf9
  > readme.md::hooks.beforeError #306c5d651315
  > source/core/retry-timing.ts::getRetryTimingHeader #2fe593155de0
  > source/errors/NetworkError.ts:7 #18c5787cbfce
  > source/types/retry.ts:33 #80b9bb5b8323
  > source/types/retry.ts:63 #b23ca3e4cb1a
#c5[overview,i5] Hooks can stop retries via ky.stop or force retries via ky.retry(), which raises a ForceRetryError that bypasses standard method checks.
  > readme.md::ky.stop #381d67bbe342
  > readme.md::"How do I retry based on the response body?" #9e0ddb131317
  > readme.md::"How do I stop retrying early?" #efee2ee86088
  > source/core/Ky.ts:698-700 #b4f3167763da
  > source/core/Ky.ts:1088-1090 #1f17f6485414
  > source/core/constants.ts:181 #ee4720aa4b59
#c6[overview,i5] Ky tracks per-request and total timeouts, aborting requests and throwing TimeoutError if limits are exceeded before or during response handling.
  > readme.md::timeout #140c6b988503
  > source/core/Ky.ts:1137-1140 #ffa1865a50c9
  > source/core/Ky.ts:1254-1258 #714583a5f3f3
