## (root)
#c9[i5] Body shortcut methods on Ky responses throw an HTTPError when response status codes are not within 200 to 299.
  > readme.md::"ky(input, options?)" #1c56f829d259
#c10[i3] When using a Request instance as input, baseUrl and prefix options are ignored.
  > readme.md::input #7a2095df1929
#c11[i2] Standard HTTP methods GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, HEAD, DELETE, and QUERY are converted to uppercase internally by Ky.
  > readme.md::method #e598f797714d
#c12[i4] The default retry limit is 2, and default retried status codes are 408, 413, 429, 500, 502, 503, and 504.
  > readme.md:264-266 #0e45ffca8cf9
#c13[i3] Setting timeout or totalTimeout to a value exceeding 2147483647 or Infinity throws a RangeError.
  > readme.md::timeout #140c6b988503
#c14[i3] The maxResponseSize option counts decompressed bytes from the stream, throwing ResponseSizeError without retrying if exceeded.
  > readme.md::maxResponseSize #01f38f174727
#c15[i3] Unlike other hooks, init hooks run synchronously, and errors thrown within them reject the returned promise without invoking beforeError hooks.
  > readme.md::hooks.init #6923bdd6675e
#c16[i3] The retryCount value passed to beforeError, afterResponse, and beforeRetry hooks begins at 0 on the initial request and increments with each retry.
  > readme.md::hooks.beforeError #306c5d651315
#c17[i4] If throwHttpErrors is set to false, error responses are treated as successful and Ky will not retry the request.
  > readme.md::throwHttpErrors #29b472f119e4
#c18[i4] Streaming upload progress in Chromium-based browsers requires an HTTP/2 or HTTP/3 connection, otherwise it fails with a network error.
  > readme.md::onUploadProgress #71289be258ff
#c19[i4] A custom fetch option passed to Ky must resolve with a Response instance, or a TypeError is thrown.
  > readme.md::fetch #d454f1ec3ff2
#c20[i3] The context option is guaranteed to always be an object, never undefined, and is shallow merged where nested objects are replaced.
  > readme.md::context #5934ac5079b7
#c21[i4] In ky.extend(), existing hooks can be removed by assigning explicit undefined, or deep-merge behavior can be overridden with replaceOption.
  > readme.md:1019 #25512816a67a
#c22[i4] Returning the ky.stop symbol from a beforeRetry hook aborts retries, returns an undefined response, and causes body parsing methods like .json() to throw a TypeError.
  > readme.md::ky.stop #381d67bbe342
#c23[i3] The delay option in ky.retry() bypasses jitter and backoffLimit, requiring a non-negative number, Infinity, or undefined.
  > readme.md::delay #4533bb2ec5f8
#c24[i3] Providing any value other than a Request object or undefined for ky.retry({ request }) causes a TypeError to be thrown.
  > readme.md::request #78531a41ce0a
#c25[i4] KyError is the base class for HTTPError, NetworkError, TimeoutError, ResponseSizeError, and ForceRetryError, but SchemaValidationError does not extend it.
  > readme.md::KyError #b0aafb673926
#c26[i4] Populating HTTPError data is constrained by request timeout (or 10 seconds if disabled), remaining totalTimeout, and a 10 MiB body limit.
  > readme.md::HTTPError #57ce31abc642
#c27[i3] If maxResponseSize is exceeded while populating error.data, Ky throws ResponseSizeError instead of HTTPError.
  > readme.md::HTTPError #57ce31abc642
#c28[i3] A connection dropping during a shortcut method like .json() is wrapped in NetworkError but is not retried.
  > readme.md::NetworkError #6d0b965ee300
#c29[i4] replaceOption wraps values so that ky.extend replaces inherited values instead of deep-merging them.
  > readme.md::replaceOption #72ebac56a0ef
#c30[i3] When retries are enabled, Ky buffers an entire streaming request body in memory to support replaying it.
  > readme.md::"Streaming request bodies" #b8a8f8bdc942
#c31[i4] Ky can retry based on response body by returning ky.retry() from an afterResponse hook even on 2xx status codes.
  > readme.md::"How do I retry based on the response body?" #9e0ddb131317
#c32[i4] Retrying can be stopped early by throwing from beforeRetry to propagate the error, or by returning ky.stop to resolve silently with undefined.
  > readme.md::"How do I stop retrying early?" #efee2ee86088
#c33[i3] Passing a function to throwHttpErrors allows selective error throwing based on HTTP response status codes.
  > readme.md::"How do I only throw on certain HTTP errors?" #ceb9846ac62a
#c34[i3] Ky can be used without a bundler by running code as an ESM JavaScript module, such as via a <script type="module"> tag.
  > readme.md::"How do I use this without a bundler like Webpack?" #1f8ccb5ece0c
#c35[i3] Ky supports the latest versions of Chrome, Firefox, and Safari.
  > readme.md::"Browser support" #5748a6086ac2
#c36[i4] Ky supports Node.js version 22 and later.
  > readme.md::"Node.js support" #ab07ac13a258
#c37[i2] Ky maintainers are Sindre Sorhus, Seth Holladay, and Szymon Marczak.
  > readme.md::Maintainers #525af71fecac
#c38[i4] Token refresh on 401 status responses can be achieved by setting retry.statusCodes to [401] and refreshing the token inside a beforeRetry hook.
  > readme.md::"How do I implement token refresh on 401 responses?" #40ee3a9c0115

## source
#c39[i4] Errors during request setup in createRequest reject the returned ResponsePromise rather than throwing synchronous exceptions.
  > source/index.ts:16 #5e01cc2a5e41
#c40[i3] When createRequest catches a setup error, it attaches body methods for all supported response types that return the rejecting promise.
  > source/index.ts::createRequest.of #664943d55fd7
#c41[i4] createInstance binds methods from requestMethods onto the Ky instance, passing the specific HTTP method into validateAndMerge.
  > source/index.ts::createInstance #748a39d6aa23
#c42[i3] ky.create creates a new KyInstance using validateAndMerge on the provided defaults.
  > source/index.ts::createInstance #748a39d6aa23
#c43[i4] ky.extend clones and validates defaults before passing them to a callback function to prevent mutating parent defaults.
  > source/index.ts::createInstance #748a39d6aa23
#c44[i2] Each Ky instance exposes stop and retry properties assigned from core constants.
  > source/index.ts::createInstance #748a39d6aa23

## source/core
#c45[i3] Ky's error response body reader caps text consumption at 10 MB and returns undefined if the total read bytes exceed it.
  > source/core/Ky.ts::readResponseText #71ed71a73433
#c46[i3] When options.baseUrl is specified, the input URL protocol must be followed by '//', or a TypeError is thrown.
