#c50[i2] Providing the legacy prefixUrl option in Ky options throws an explicit Error indicating it was renamed to prefix in v2.
  > source/core/Ky.ts:469-471 #073f5ffd5268
#c51[i4] Setting options.json automatically serializes the body and sets the 'content-type' header to 'application/json' unless explicitly provided by the user.
  > source/core/Ky.ts:527-532 #22608af7f8fe
#c52[i3] If a beforeRetry hook returns ky.stop, calling body-reading methods on the response promise throws a TypeError.
  > source/core/Ky.ts::Ky.create.of #862c20e7fd9c
#c53[i4] Responses returned by beforeRequest hooks that trigger an HTTPError are immediately thrown and never retried.
  > source/core/Ky.ts:638-640 #7b453a9e05d3
#c54[i4] Forced retries triggered via isForceRetryError skip standard HTTP method checks and retry.shouldRetry callbacks.
  > source/core/Ky.ts:698-700 #b4f3167763da
#c55[i3] Errors originating from beforeRetry hooks are tracked and bypass beforeError hook processing.
  > source/core/Ky.ts:790-792 #2466c70c17e1
#c56[i3] When options.timeout is false, the timeout for reading error response data defaults to 10,000 milliseconds.
  > source/core/Ky.ts:856 #15abaf96f841
#c57[i3] If a throwHttpErrors function predicate throws an exception, Ky cancels the response body before rethrowing the error.
  > source/core/Ky.ts:1022-1027 #6458d4b34865
#c58[i4] If an afterResponse hook returns a retry marker, Ky converts it to a ForceRetryError.
  > source/core/Ky.ts:1088-1090 #1f17f6485414
#c59[i4] When the calculated retry delay equals or exceeds remainingTotalTimeout, Ky delays for the remaining time and throws TimeoutError without sending another request.
  > source/core/Ky.ts:1137-1140 #ffa1865a50c9
#c60[i4] If a `beforeRetry` hook returns a `Response`, Ky tracks it in `#hookResponses`, increments `#retryCount`, and returns it directly.
  > source/core/Ky.ts:1196-1200 #8a1697d9703e
#c61[i4] Returning `stop` from a `beforeRetry` hook stops the retry process and returns undefined.
  > source/core/Ky.ts:1203-1205 #5a8a2993ec3c
#c62[i4] Ky only clones the request for retry if retry limit is greater than 0, avoiding `ReadableStream#tee()` stream buffering overhead when retries are disabled.
  > source/core/Ky.ts:1225 #064fa0713be2
#c63[i3] The custom `fetch` function must resolve with a `Response`, or Ky throws a `TypeError`.
  > source/core/Ky.ts:1250-1252 #b9e32ed91641
#c64[i4] When total timeout is exhausted after fetch or during an error, Ky aborts `#abortController` and throws a `TimeoutError`.
  > source/core/Ky.ts:1254-1258 #714583a5f3f3
#c65[i3] Ky intercepts catch blocks and throws if the user abort signal has been triggered to prevent Chromium from misidentifying user aborts as network errors.
  > source/core/Ky.ts:1262 #d22311019643
#c66[i3] Ky validates that options returned from `beforeRetry` hooks are objects containing only allowed keys from `beforeRetryOptionKeys`.
  > source/core/Ky.ts:1292-1296 #55c5793840d9
#c67[i3] `#wrapRequestWithUploadProgress` transforms the request using `streamRequest` only if `onUploadProgress` is set, `supportsRequestStreams` is true, and `request.body` exists.
  > source/core/Ky.ts:1370-1372 #6e501a58ff2f
#c68[i3] Ky detects request stream support by testing Request constructor stream handling with duplex access, accounting for Bun and Deno environments.
