#c76[i4] Retry-After and X-RateLimit-Retry-After disable timestamp parsing, whereas RateLimit-Reset, X-RateLimit-Reset, and X-Rate-Limit-Reset set allowTimestamp to true.
  > source/core/retry-timing.ts::getRetryTimingHeader #2fe593155de0
#c77[i4] Numeric values are treated as epoch timestamps instead of delays only when allowTimestamp is true and the value is at least 1_000_000_000 seconds.
  > source/core/retry-timing.ts::calculateRetryTimingDelay #5ad0cabe55b3
#c78[i3] Date parsing only supports IMF-fixdate, RFC 850, and asctime formats, returning undefined for other strings.
