[probes]
?p1 What is the default per-attempt timeout in milliseconds for Ky requests?
  = 10000
  > readme.md::timeout #140c6b988503
?p2 What happens if a custom fetch function does not resolve with a Response object?
  = A TypeError is thrown.
  > readme.md::fetch #d454f1ec3ff2
?p3 What error does Ky throw if totalTimeout expires while error.data is being populated?
  = TimeoutError
  > readme.md::HTTPError #57ce31abc642
?p4 What does a request resolve with if ky.stop is returned from a beforeRetry hook?
  = undefined
  > readme.md::"How do I stop retrying early?" #efee2ee86088
?p5 What is the maximum allowed error response body size in bytes before Ky cancels reading and returns undefined?
  = 10 * 1024 * 1024 (10 MB)
  > source/core/Ky.ts::maxErrorResponseBodySize #bc64f4409a42
?p6 What error is thrown if retry.delay returns a non-number or negative value?
  = A TypeError stating '`retry.delay` must return a non-negative number or `Infinity`'.
  > source/core/Ky.ts:671 #5cca18357bd8
?p7 What error does Ky throw if a raw network error occurs inside `#fetch`?
  = NetworkError (wrapping the original error as cause)
  > source/core/Ky.ts:1268-1270 #4069bd1e020e
?p8 What is the numeric value of maxSafeTimeout in Ky?
  = 2147483647
  > source/core/constants.ts::maxSafeTimeout #939ac08d2afe
?p9 What is the minimum numeric second threshold required for an allowed header value to be treated as an epoch timestamp?
  = 1_000_000_000 (representing 2001-09-09)
  > source/core/retry-timing.ts::timestampThresholdSeconds #f575080c976f
?p10 What error message is produced when null is passed into ForceRetryError's constructor?
  = The `ky.retry()` options must be an object
  > source/errors/ForceRetryError.ts::ForceRetryError.constructor #f5ab0764aa8e
?p11 What is the timeout duration for error.data body reads and parsing if the timeout option is disabled?
  = 10 seconds
  > source/errors/HTTPError.ts:9 #28c0380f4a51
?p12 Which specific error classes extend KyError?
  = HTTPError, NetworkError, TimeoutError, ResponseSizeError, and ForceRetryError.
  > source/errors/KyError.ts:2 #d2fe4a0de19d
?p13 Why is a dropped connection while reading a response body via .json() not retried even though it is wrapped in NetworkError?
  = Because the response has already been received.
  > source/errors/NetworkError.ts:7 #18c5787cbfce
?p14 What does NonError.wrap return if the provided value is already an Error?
  = The value as-is.
  > source/errors/NonError.ts::NonError #1a1ad421dfb3
?p15 What message format does ResponseSizeError pass to its superclass constructor?
  = Response body exceeded ${maxResponseSize} bytes: ${request.method} ${request.url}
  > source/errors/ResponseSizeError.ts::ResponseSizeError.constructor #20201d86fd71
?p16 Why does SchemaValidationError avoid extending KyError?
  = It does not represent a failure in Ky's HTTP lifecycle since the request succeeded and only the user's schema rejected the data.
  > source/errors/SchemaValidationError.ts:6 #a78383935ccd
?p17 What message does the TimeoutError constructor pass to super()?
  = `Request timed out: ${request.method} ${request.url}`
  > source/errors/TimeoutError.ts::TimeoutError.constructor #3d06a554892b
?p18 Why does createRequest catch setup errors and return a rejected promise instead of letting them throw?
  = To match fetch() reporting and ensure callers only have one error channel to handle.
  > source/index.ts:16 #5e01cc2a5e41
?p19 What error does ResponsePromise's body shortcut throw if the response status is outside 200...299?
  = An HTTPError.
  > source/types/ResponsePromise.ts:2 #2e4b2575614a
?p20 What constraint must BaseType satisfy in LiteralUnion?
  = BaseType must extend Primitive.
  > source/types/common.ts::LiteralUnion #40b4101207f5
?p21 What happens if a beforeRetry hook returns `{options: {...}}` with an omitted option versus setting it to `undefined`?
  = Omitted options retain their current value, while `undefined` restores Ky's default value rather than settings from `ky.create()` or `ky.extend()`.
  > source/types/hooks.ts:210 #d1cb5b86b00f
?p22 What error occurs if body methods like .json() are called on a request aborted via ky.stop?
  = A TypeError is thrown because there is no response to parse.
  > source/types/ky.ts:128 #9e07b1d28551
?p23 What happens when parseJson is called in terms of the arguments passed to it?
  = It receives the response text as the first argument and a context object containing request and response as the second argument.
  > source/types/options.ts:58 #9e80e3358217
?p24 What is the default type parameter for the generic J in KyRequest's json method?
  = T
  > source/types/request.ts::KyRequest #c1c59947097d
?p25 What standard type does KyResponse intersect with?
  = Response
  > source/types/response.ts::KyResponse #ec9a528b6ea3
?p26 What is the default exponential backoff delay formula in RetryOptions?
  = attemptCount => 0.3 * (2 ** (attemptCount - 1)) * 1000
  > source/types/retry.ts:82 #4a4e3386b42c
?p27 What literal number type is required for '~standard'.version in StandardSchemaV1?
  = 1
  > source/types/standard-schema.ts::StandardSchemaV1 #f17ca6260782
?p28 Which HTTP status codes are classified as nullBodyStatuses?
  = 101, 103, 204, 205, and 304.
  > source/utils/body.ts::nullBodyStatuses #8dc7fb324520
?p29 What method is called on signal at the start of delay if signal is provided?
  = signal.throwIfAborted()
  > source/utils/delay.ts::delay #446c2a0ec5f0
?p30 What error name must an error have to be considered a valid raw network error?
  = TypeError
  > source/utils/is-network-error.ts::isRawNetworkError #804cf994a8eb
